  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreRC 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "When organizing study information, you make note of the early safety
    findings, including the dosing range and the side effects observed in animal
    models.\n\n<b>In this scenario, what is the research coordinator\u2019s role
    in preclinical research?</b>"
  explanation: "During preclinical research, research coordinators play an important
    role in preparing for next steps by organizing study information, documenting
    key findings, and flagging details\u2014such as early safety observations or
    dosing notes\u2014that may be important later, especially if the research moves
    forward to clinical trials. Their careful record-keeping helps ensure that, if
    the research moves forward, clinical teams have clear, reliable information to
    build on."
  correctAnswer: Organizing and documenting important information from preclinical
    studies
  incorrectAnswer1: Writing the clinical trial protocol and designing the study
  incorrectAnswer2: Recruiting patients to participate in the clinical trial
  incorrectAnswer3: Testing the new treatment in patients to confirm early findings
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
